From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:59:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: keep the J713-only
 sleep words

macOS on the J604 writes none of the eight power state words the
T8132 sleep raises for the commit: DWI stays on under AUTO_ENABLE, and
the other seven are in no J604 node and in none of the words macOS
touches from boot to idle. List all eight in apple,ps-keep-on.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 0dd5c26808..3a964b0400 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -436,5 +436,11 @@ opp-4464000000 {
 
 /* Deep sleep: the T8132 sleep controller, as the J713 enables it upstream. */
 &sleep {
+	/*
+	 * The J713's macOS has these at f at the commit; the J604's macOS
+	 * writes none of them before it (q-pwr-s2r-1), DWI stays on under
+	 * AUTO_ENABLE, and the other seven are in no J604 node.
+	 */
+	apple,ps-keep-on = <0x118 0x2f8 0x310 0x318 0x320 0x348 0x358 0x368>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
-- 
